+    allowlist answers *where* a patch may write; this screen answers *what kind
+    of filesystem object* it may produce.  It is also reused by the eval apply
+    seam, because evaluating an unreviewed binary/symlink patch would otherwise
+    give the patch a different privilege envelope than the live deploy path.
+
+    The parser is strict around Git's extended headers but deliberately permits
+    ordinary unified diffs without Git metadata, which are a supported input to
+    ``git apply``.  Any recognized type/mode header outside the single regular
+    mode is rejected fail-closed.
